[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3120532196","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102047#issuecomment-3120532196","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102047","id":3120532196,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc65_4rk","user":{"login":"CarterG81","id":17555008,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTU1MDA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17555008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CarterG81","html_url":"https://github.com/CarterG81","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CarterG81/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CarterG81/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CarterG81/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CarterG81/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CarterG81/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CarterG81/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CarterG81/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CarterG81/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CarterG81/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-25T22:13:12Z","updated_at":"2025-07-25T22:14:09Z","body":"It would also be a workaround if we allowed for the selectable portion of any gameobject to be defined as well. Then we don't even have to worry about locking/unlocking the larger nodes (which can be a huge PITA when forgetting to relock after editing).\n\nThanks for opening this issue. I find a lot of trouble here since I use a mask. The 'select' tool constantly grabs the wrong gameobject because the invisible portion is so much larger. I thought locking the node would fix it, but nope - not unless I open \"editable children\" on every single object in my scene, since they almost all use masks. Ugh.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"http